"text": "What the two 100 m bands can see - Source: band tags — 12 \"Detrended elevation — topography with regional trends removed\", 19 \"Detrended elevation slope — gradient of elevation after detrending\". - Relevance: Detrending is right for scarp work, but a 100 m pixel averages 10,000 m² of ground; a 2 m scarp 20 m wide is diluted roughly fifty-fold. Bands 12/19 resolve range fronts and large piedmont lineaments and miss small recent scarps. - Confidence: verified for band tags; the dilution reasoning is inference."
